        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 47:3",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 47,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "As for our redeemer, the Lord of hosts is his name, the Holy One of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 41
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 47:4",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 47,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Sit thou silent, and get thee into darkness, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called, The lady of kingdoms.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "IE you are going into exile."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 47:5",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 47,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "I was wroth with my people, I have polluted mine inheritance, and given them into thine hand: thou didst shew them no mercy; upon the ancient hast thou very heavily laid thy yoke.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "IE Israel’s Babylonian captivity is predicted."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Isaiah 47:6",
        "book": "Isaiah",
        "chapter": 47,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And thou saidst, I shall be a lady for ever: so that thou didst not lay these things to thy heart, neither didst remember the latter end of it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "OR a mistress."
          },
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 136,
